  'our sd(p)' IS the Brier resolution term (its square).
  'achievable' adds the missing between-start spread to each
  start's own mean and re-reads the probability, so it is what
  this same simulator would produce if it differentiated starts
  as much as reality does. share < 100% is unpriced signal.

